,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.880917873,"data":"  [battery  988.7s] ==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.881688184,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]   5. what this does NOT say\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.882558333,"data":"  [battery  988.7s] ==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.883372583,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]   * No whole-step number is a denominator anywhere above. The\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.88417688,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     reference's whole step is printed as CONTEXT only: it is 7\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.884952374,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     launches, five of them state updates.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.88579462,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]   * The ratio against the reference is render-against-render, both\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.886646816,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     producing the same uint8 observation at the same batch on the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.887472321,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     same card. If the digests differ, the ratio is between two\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.888224643,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     different computations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.888996351,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]   * The clean-vs-faithful delta is the crossing cost. It is the only\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.889725466,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     number here that no other arm in this study has.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.890529264,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]   * Every ms above is DEVICE time: the sum of the per-kernel device\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.891337801,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     times in the graph, measured with tinygrad's own time_call, host\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.892113328,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     tracing excluded. The host build+realize number printed beside it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.892831704,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     is context and is NOT comparable to the reference's, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.893614816,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     reference pays no tracing cost. Calling realize() on an already\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.894476699,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     realized tensor is a no-op; time_graph raises if handed one,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.895292154,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     because an earlier version of this file did exactly that and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.896097447,"data":"  [battery  988.7s]     reported the port as 13x FASTER than the hand-written CUDA.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.896913826,"data":"  [battery  988.7s] \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1449.897705988,"data":"  [battery  988.8s] wrote /kaggle/working/faithful_battery.json\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.272650618,"data":"  [battery] exit 0 after 991.1s\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.273904501,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.27548552,"data":"--- 8. the three-way table, and the clean-vs-faithful delta ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.277314493,"data":"   batch      ref us    clean ms    faith ms   f/clean  clean/ref  faith/ref   kernels c/f  same obs\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.27837588,"data":"           (DEVICE time; host tracing excluded -- see battery section 5)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.279991424,"data":"     512       155.6      16.115      17.200     1.067     110.15     117.57         42/42  True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.281241815,"data":"    1024       284.6       3.012      10.442     3.466      10.43      36.16         10/10  True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.282271559,"data":"    2048       561.2       5.642      20.715     3.672      10.04      36.87         10/10  True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.283547486,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.284850135,"data":"--- what these numbers are, and are not ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.286119431,"data":"  * The three columns are RENDERS. Same world, same cameras, same\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.287210996,"data":"    max_steps, same uint8 observation, same card, same run, equal batch.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.28833673,"data":"    `f/clean` is the crossing cost and is the number this arm adds; the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.289392516,"data":"    two `*/ref` columns are render-against-render and are the same\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.290591907,"data":"    comparison `notes/19` §5.2 makes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.29170446,"data":"  * The two ms columns are DEVICE time -- the sum of the per-kernel\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.293021397,"data":"    device times in the graph, measured with tinygrad's own time_call,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.294338093,"data":"    host tracing excluded. The reference's us figure is a cudaEvent\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.295350968,"data":"    median around a single launch, which is also device time and is the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.296377497,"data":"    like-for-like comparison. The host build+realize figure printed\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.297615779,"data":"    beside each row is CONTEXT: it includes the framework's graph\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.298843352,"data":"    tracing, which the reference does not pay, so it is NOT divided by\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.299990503,"data":"    anything here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.301467703,"data":"  * Calling realize() on an already-realized tensor is a silent no-op.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.302566813,"data":"    An earlier version of battery.py timed exactly that and reported the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.303691649,"data":"    port at 0.011 ms against the reference's 152 us -- a 13x speedup over\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.304820855,"data":"    hand-written CUDA, from a graph whose offline SASS is tens of times\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.305988051,"data":"    the reference's instruction count. time_graph now raises if handed a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.307289868,"data":"    realized tensor, and the timing instrument is minecu_tg's own\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.308957813,"data":"    linear_device_time_ms, which is the code path `notes/19` measured\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.310249882,"data":"    with. That false number is the reason the clock is named on every\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.311850415,"data":"    row rather than in a footnote.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.312839016,"data":"  * The reference's whole-step figure is printed for context and is NOT a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.313869822,"data":"    denominator anywhere. `4.55 M env-steps/s` covers 7 launches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.314932882,"data":"  * `same obs` compares the two modes' observations by sha256. Both are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.315935905,"data":"    verified against the same float64 transcription and the same naive\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.316966697,"data":"    port, so a False here would mean the crossings changed the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.318051009,"data":"    computation, and the ratios above it would be between two different\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.319308855,"data":"    computations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.320354006,"data":"  * The ratio to the reference is NOT attributed to the compiler unless\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.32136904,"data":"    both sides did the same work. Each mode's mean steps/pixel is in the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.322462416,"data":"    battery output. The reference's own DEVICE-side step count is NOT\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.323523012,"data":"    available here: it needs the dda_probe_kernel from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.324636215,"data":"    minecu_ref/bench/bench.cu, which refdrv.cu does not link, and putting\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.325721755,"data":"    the CPU model's number under the same label would be a claim about a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.326993212,"data":"    device that was not measured. The workload check is one-sided and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.328020707,"data":"    the note says so rather than rounding it up.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.329148592,"data":"  * The obs_sha256 in the battery is this port's. verify.py proved it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.330099696,"data":"    equals the naive port's and a float64 transcription's ON THIS CARD in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.331112015,"data":"    this run. It is NOT compared against the reference's dumped bytes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.331995922,"data":"    here; that is notes/19's comparison on the reference's own state, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.333066729,"data":"    this arm did not re-derive it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.335176255,"data":"  * No SASS number is reported here. The instruction and register counts\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.336086438,"data":"    come from the offline archlab route on the host, where ptxas and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.33757466,"data":"    cuobjdump exist and nvcc's version is pinned; the T4 image's CUDA\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.33874974,"data":"    version is recorded but not used for a count.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1452.33992105,"data":"\n"}
